    {
      "title": "Mutation Toolkit Overview",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Mutation Toolkit Overview",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Three Tools",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Server Action}: async function marked `'use server'`, runs on the server",
                "Called from forms or client code; Next.js exposes a ==POST endpoint== for it",
                "{green:Route Handler}: `route.ts` exporting ==GET/POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE/HEAD/OPTIONS==",
                "Builds a public HTTP endpoint on Web `Request`/`Response`",
                "{purple:Middleware}: runs ==before the request completes==, matched by path",
                "Jobs: redirect, rewrite, set headers, gate access"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "'use server'",
                "export async function save(fd: FormData) {",
                "  const title = fd.get('title')",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "Server Action in its own file"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Which One to Use",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Tool"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Mutation from your own UI",
                  "{blue:Server Action}"
                ],
                [
                  "Webhook, public API, non-UI client",
                  "{green:Route Handler}"
                ],
                [
                  "Cross-cutting check before rendering",
                  "{purple:Middleware}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Segment Conflict",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "One owner per route",
              "text": "A `route.ts` cannot sit beside a `page.tsx` at the same ==route segment==. They **conflict**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Server Actions and Forms",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Server Actions and Forms",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Define and Wire",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==`'use server'`== inline in a Server Component, or atop a file",
                "`<form action={fn}>` passes ==FormData==: `formData.get('name')`",
                "Forms work before hydration (==progressive enhancement==)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "ts",
              "lines": [
                "'use server'",
                "export async function create(prev, fd) {",
                "  const title = fd.get('title')",
                "  // validate, auth, write",
                "  redirect('/posts')",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. State, Pending, Safety",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`useActionState(action, init)` → `[state, formAction, pending]`",
                "`useFormStatus` in a ==child== reads `pending`",
                "Actions are ==public POST endpoints==: validate (zod), re-check auth"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Validate",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Auth",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Write DB",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Revalidate",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "redirect",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes and Interview Point",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "redirect() throws",
              "text": "Never wrap `redirect()` in try/catch; call it ==after== the catch."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Is an action private?** No, public POST: validate and check auth inside",
                "**Why not try/catch redirect?** It throws internally; the catch swallows it",
                "**Where does pending come from?** `useActionState`, or `useFormStatus` in a child"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Revalidation After Mutations",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Revalidation After Mutations",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Two Ways to Invalidate",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`revalidatePath('/posts')`: ==invalidate== that route's data and output on the next visit",
                "Second arg `'layout'` or `'page'` scopes it: `revalidatePath('/', 'layout')`",
                "`revalidateTag('posts', 'max')`: invalidate every entry tagged `posts`",
                "One-argument `revalidateTag('posts')` is ==deprecated== in Next.js 16",
                "`updateTag('posts')`: read-your-writes inside a Server Action"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Order of Steps",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Validate",
                    "note": "input and auth",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Write DB",
                    "note": "must succeed",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Invalidate",
                    "note": "path or tag",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Redirect",
                    "note": "optional",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "// read: tag the fetch",
                "fetch(url, { next: { tags: ['posts'] } })",
                "// Server Action, after the write",
                "revalidateTag('posts', 'max')"
              ],
              "note": "same string tags and invalidates"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Path vs Tag",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Path",
                "Tag"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Style",
                  "Simple, route-oriented",
                  "Precise"
                ],
                [
                  "Reach",
                  "One route or subtree",
                  "Every route using that data"
                ],
                [
                  "Needs",
                  "Nothing extra",
                  "Tagged fetch"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No invalidation after a mutation leaves ==stale data== in the UI",
                "`revalidatePath('/')` alone skips nested routes; add `'layout'`",
                "Calling it during render: use only in Server Actions or Route Handlers"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Route Handlers (route.ts)",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Route Handlers (route.ts)",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Define the Handler",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "File: ==app/api/items/route.ts== (any segment)",
                "Export ==named async functions== per method: `GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`, `HEAD`, `OPTIONS`",
                "Return `Response.json(data, { status: 201 })` or `new Response(body, { headers })`",
                "`NextResponse` adds helpers: ==cookies==, ==redirects=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Params and Input",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "// app/api/items/[id]/route.ts",
                "export async function POST(request: Request,",
                "  { params }: { params: Promise<{ id: string }> }) {",
                "  const { id } = await params",
                "  const body = await request.json()",
                "  return Response.json({ id, body }, { status: 201 })",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "params is a Promise in recent versions: await it"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Read",
                "API"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "JSON body",
                  "`await request.json()`"
                ],
                [
                  "Form body",
                  "`await request.formData()`"
                ],
                [
                  "Raw body",
                  "`await request.text()`"
                ],
                [
                  "Query",
                  "`new URL(request.url).searchParams`"
                ],
                [
                  "Query (NextRequest)",
                  "`request.nextUrl.searchParams`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Caching Gotcha",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "GET handlers are ==not cached by default== in current versions",
                "Opt in: `export const dynamic = 'force-static'`",
                "Reading `request` or `cookies` makes it {orange:dynamic} anyway"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Segment clash",
              "text": "A `route.ts` cannot sit beside a `page.tsx` in the same segment: they ==conflict==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Request/Response APIs and Middleware",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Request/Response APIs and Middleware",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Request Helpers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`cookies()` and `headers()` are ==async==: await them",
                "`cookies().set` / `delete`: only in {green:Actions} and {green:Route Handlers}, not render"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "const jar = await cookies()",
                "const h = await headers()"
              ],
              "note": "read both on the server; set only in actions or handlers"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Adds"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`NextRequest`",
                  "`nextUrl`, `cookies`"
                ],
                [
                  "`NextResponse`",
                  "`json` `redirect` `rewrite` `next`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Middleware and proxy",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Next.js 16: `middleware.ts` is ==deprecated==, renamed `proxy.ts`",
                "`proxy.ts` exports `proxy(request)`; runs on {green:Node.js}",
                "Root or `src/`; `config.matcher` limits paths",
                "Jobs: auth redirect, locale rewrite, headers; keep it light",
                "Edge limits (no Node-only APIs) apply only to old `middleware.ts`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "export function proxy(req: NextRequest) {",
                "  return NextResponse.redirect(new URL('/login', req.url))",
                "}",
                "export const config = { matcher: ['/dashboard/:path*'] }"
              ],
              "note": "old file: same shape, function named middleware"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never auth in middleware alone",
              "text": "Matchers can miss routes and actions are directly callable. Re-verify in Actions, Handlers and data access."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Which Tool and Key Snippets",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Which Tool and Key Snippets",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Which Tool",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Own form or button mutation",
                  "{green:Server Action}"
                ],
                [
                  "Webhook, third-party or mobile client",
                  "{blue:Route Handler}"
                ],
                [
                  "Pre-render redirect, rewrite, header",
                  "{purple:Middleware}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Skeletons",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Action: ==validate==, ==auth check==, write DB, revalidate, redirect"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "ts",
              "lines": [
                "'use server'",
                "export async function create(prev, formData) {",
                "  // validate, auth check, write DB",
                "  revalidatePath('/x')",
                "  redirect('/x')",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Handler: read the body, return a `Response` with a status"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "ts",
              "lines": [
                "export async function POST(req: Request) {",
                "  const body = await req.json()",
                "  return Response.json({ ok: true }, { status: 201 })",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Revalidate and Middleware",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`revalidatePath('/p', 'layout')`: whole subtree",
                "`revalidateTag('t', 'max')`: tagged fetches (one-arg form deprecated in 16)",
                "`updateTag('t')`: read-your-writes inside a Server Action",
                "Tag a fetch with `next: { tags: ['t'] }`",
                "Middleware returns `NextResponse.redirect(new URL('/login', req.url))`",
                "Limit paths with `config.matcher`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Checklist",
              "text": "==Validate==, ==authorize==, ==revalidate==. Never wrap `redirect()` in try/catch."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Spot the bug: an action runs `try { await save(); redirect('/posts') } catch { return { error: 'Failed' } }`. What does the user see on success?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The error message, even though the save worked",
                "`redirect()` throws internally, so the `catch` swallows it",
                "Fix: call `redirect` after the try/catch"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "An action edits /blog/[slug] and calls `revalidatePath('/')`. Why might /blog/hello still be stale?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`'/'` alone refreshes only that page, not nested routes",
                "Use `revalidatePath('/', 'layout')`, or `revalidateTag` on a tagged fetch"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Middleware redirects logged-out users away from /dashboard/:path*. Is `deleteAccount` on that page safe without its own check?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No: actions are public POST endpoints, directly callable",
                "Matchers can miss routes, so re-check auth inside the action"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}